      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a bit vague, but if you look at cases where states block certain platforms to prevent riots or stop the spread of dangerous misinformation that could cause real-world violence, doesn't that fall under legitimate social stability? it seems like the \"freedom\" argument gets used a lot to defend things that are actually just harmful.",
